# 03. NEW MODEL DISCOVERY — TARANEH-ASR

A potentially important candidate was identified in recent research.

Repository:

https://github.com/areffarhadi/persian-asr

Model family:

```text
Taraneh-WBase
Taraneh-WMedium
Taraneh-WLarge
Taraneh-Q0.6B
Taraneh-Q1.7B
```

The authors report that the models were fine-tuned on approximately 1,560 hours of Persian speech.

The repository includes a Persian forced-alignment implementation using selected transformer attention heads and dynamic time warping.

The documented alignment command includes:

```bash
python scripts/infer.py \
  --model Taraneh-WMedium \
  --audio input.wav \
  --output_dir results/ \
  --task asr+fa
```

According to the current repository documentation:

- WMedium, WLarge, Q0.6B, and Q1.7B support the `asr+fa` path.
- WBase is documented as ASR-only.
- Whisper-based alignment uses decoder cross-attention.
- Qwen-based alignment uses thinker self-attention.
- DTW generates the alignment path.
- Alignment does not constitute a separately trained DTW model.

The repository reports these FarsDat results:

| Candidate | Reported boundary MAE |
|---|---:|
| Taraneh-WMedium | 37.8 ms |
| Taraneh-WLarge | 38.1 ms |
| Taraneh-Q0.6B | 47.2 ms |
| Taraneh-Q1.7B | 48.5 ms |

The repository describes MIT licensing for its Whisper-based checkpoints and Apache-2.0 for its Qwen-based checkpoints.

These are author-reported results and licensing claims.

They are NOT independent AvaPardaz verification.

